00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:13,520
169, 170, 171, 172

15
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,880
194, 195, 196

16
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,600
199, 200

17
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,160
Li Yiran.

18
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:30,080
Chen Baixi.

19
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,720
Why are you here?

20
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,200
Passing by. Taking a walk.

21
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,600
Just strolling.

22
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,560
Took a wrong turn.

23
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:39,960
What's the matter?

24
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:40,720
None of your business.

25
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,520
Who cares about you?

26
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,600
You're the one who called me.

27
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,520
Where... where's my sister?

28
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,960
Doing homework on my roof.

29
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,880
Let's go. I'll take you to her.

30
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,440
Hey,

31
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,800
you don't even have waiters here?

32
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:16,120
Sir, this isn't a restaurant.

33
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,440
Why would we need waiters?

34
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,160
Sorry about that.

35
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:19,880
Xiaofang.

36
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,280
I'm so sorry.

37
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,000
What kind of services are you looking for, sir?

38
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,560
Little punk, are you the waiter?

39
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,360
Get me a bottle of Perrier.

40
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,200
Chilled, thanks.

41
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,840
He wants a Perrier.

42
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,160
I'm sorry, sir.

43
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,920
We only have this.

44
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:41,920
You'll have to make do.

45
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,080
Country bumpkin.

46
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,960
Have you booked a funeral service?

47
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,760
My mom already booked one for my grandpa.

48
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,920
I'm just here today

49
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:51,360
to confirm the arrangements.

50
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,000
May I have your last name?

51
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,480
My last name is Zhuang.

52
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,880
Zhuang.

53
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,040
Zhuang Qiang really likes to show off.

54
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:01,560
Only good-looking guys are called players.

55
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:03,120
Him?

56
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:05,320
He's a wannabe player at best.

57
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:09,520
Let me tell you,

58
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,680
my grandpa is a prominent figure in this village.

59
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:14,280
His funeral has to be grand.

60
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,320
Money is no object.

61
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:23,000
Then please take a look at the funeral process.

62
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:30,280
Let me start by explaining the hearse.

63
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,040
Your process is way too simple.

64
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:34,880
My grandpa loved opera when he was alive.

65
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,600
And you don't even have an opera troupe.

66
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:39,560
We can arrange that.

67
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,760
But it's not included in the standard package.

68
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,680
If you want it, there will be an extra charge.

69
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,560
Not just an opera troupe,

70
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,120
as long as you're willing to pay,

71
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,360
even singers and celebrities,

72
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,960
we can hire them for you.

73
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:52,080
That's so expensive!

74
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,600
You're basically robbing people, you know?

75
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,080
Forget it, forget it.

76
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:59,240
I think playing some dirges will be just fine.

77
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:05,080
Do you have any other requests?

78
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,080
Alright, that's it.

79
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:09,320
You're too unprofessional to pull it off anyway.

80
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:10,920
I think

81
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,840
we'll just stick to the plan.

82
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,320
I'm leaving.

83
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:21,640
Everyone!

84
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:25,040
Wu Huilian made Chongqing Spicy Chicken for you all!

85
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:29,920
Ranran!

86
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:33,960
Ranran!

87
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,320
Manager Wang, thank you so much.

88
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,400
The setup looks amazing.

89
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,080
With our strong partnership this time,

90
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:53,920
it'll definitely be a hit.

91
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:56,360
President Zhou, you're too kind.

92
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,360
Your company hosting the wedding here

93
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:00,840
really boosts our popularity.

94
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:01,640
It's a win-win.

95
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:02,720
Pleasure working with you.

96
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,480
Pleasure working with you.

97
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,200
Goodbye.

98
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,240
Here, Ranran.

99
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,160
Eat up.

100
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,040
All these dishes

101
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,560
are your old favorites.

102
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,280
Thanks.

103
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,280
But seeing you is a turn-off.

104
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,200
Just get to the point.

105
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:26,920
Ranran, I know

106
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:28,720
I hurt you deeply.

107
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:31,360
But I never expected you'd just give up and move back home,

108
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,520
and even start dealing with the dead.

109
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,280
There's a lot you'd never expect.

110
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,560
What future does a funeral home in this small town have?

111
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:39,640
There's no way you can fulfill your true potential.

112
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:41,760
What do you mean no future?

113
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,560
It does.

114
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,000
The day you drop dead,

115
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,360
I can give you a proper send-off.

116
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,520
Ranran.

117
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,440
Actually, Linda and I broke up a long time ago.

118
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,200
You're still the only one in my heart.

119
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,360
Whether you two broke up or not,

120
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,240
I don't give a damn.

121
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:03,240
Ranran, I came back this time just for you.

122
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,000
Let's just put the past behind us.

123
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:05,520
Okay?

124
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:06,640
Are you kidding me?

125
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,160
You came back for me?

126
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,200
Didn't you come back because your grandpa passed away?

127
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,320
What?

128
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,280
Did Linda dump you,

129
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:13,440
so you came here for comfort?

130
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,720
Psycho.

131
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,240
Ranran.

132
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,280
Come back to Shanghai with me.

133
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,520
Okay?

134
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,360
What do you take me for?

135
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:24,520
A recycling bin?

136
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,720
You think I take in any kind of trash?

137
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,280
Ranran, I'm saying this for your own good.

138
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,360
Can't you hear that?

139
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:28,880
For my own good?

140
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,040
Then stay away from me,

141
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,960
and don't ever show your face to me again.

142
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,480
Ranran.

143
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,840
You haven't changed a bit after all these years.

144
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,480
You still love being so pushy.

145
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,320
You haven't changed a bit either.

146
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,000
You're still just as full of yourself.

147
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:47,280
Ranran.

148
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,040
Ranran.

149
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:52,280
Ranran.

150
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:53,920
Ranran.

151
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:57,480
I'm sorry. Stop being angry.

152
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,480
Forgive me, please?

153
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,800
You're disgusting!

154
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,000
I know I was wrong. I'm sorry.

155
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:06,200
Let's go back to how we were, okay?

156
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:07,920
Let's go back to the past.

157
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:10,320
Get lost.

158
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,480
Unbelievable! Unbelievable!

159
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,040
Big news! Big news!

160
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,560
Brother-in-law! Xiaofang!

161
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,320
Guess what I just saw!

162
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:25,720
"Big news," you say?

163
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,800
You're a walking spectacle yourself.

164
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:30,240
I saw Yiran hugging some guy!

165
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,920
Hugging?

166
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,120
Brother-in-law.

167
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:35,880
What are you gonna do?

168
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:37,080
Me?

169
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,000
That's her freedom.

170
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:42,080
Free...

171
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,440
Hold on a second.

172
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:46,360
Yiran and that damn scumbag Zhuang Qiang?

173
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,520
Hugging?

174
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,480
A scumbag?

175
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:50,120
Yiran dated a scumbag?

176
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,160
That's her ex-boyfriend.

177
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,160
Her ex-boyfriend?

178
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,800
Then it makes sense.

179
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,160
They must've rekindled an old flame.

180
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,600
Rekindle an old flame?

181
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,560
Tell us!

182
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,880
What did you see?

183
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:03,600
I saw...

184
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:03,920
Xiaofang.

185
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,040
I can't even explain it to you.

186
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,480
This batch of mums isn't that good.

187
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,400
Bro Amin!

188
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:11,040
Come here.

189
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,080
Help me act it out for them.

190
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:16,800
No way, no way.

191
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:17,880
You can do it.

192
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:19,560
Help my brother-in-law out!

193
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:23,720
Come on, come on.

194
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,200
I'll recreate the scene for you guys.

195
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,800
Here's how it went down.

196
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:30,240
Now, I'll be that...

197
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:30,880
scumbag.

198
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,080
And you'll be Yiran.

199
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:33,840
Me?

200
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:35,720
Action!

201
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,160
Ranran.

202
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,360
After you left,

203
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,520
I realized how much I love you.

204
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,200
Then what were you doing when we broke up?

205
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,520
Broke up...

206
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,440
You... Take a few steps!

207
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,360
Step forward a bit.

208
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,120
Ranran,

209
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,360
I don't care if it's the ends of the earth.

210
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,120
Wherever you are,

211
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:08,640
I'll go.

212
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,680
You liar!

213
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,040
Ranran,

214
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,920
I will never let go of your hand again.

215
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,720
Do you really mean that?

216
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:20,800
I do.

217
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,800
Every word of it is true.

218
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:25,240
We will never be apart again.

219
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,520
Only when mountains crumble

220
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:30,400
will I leave you.

221
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:32,040
Stop acting!

222
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,480
You two are so gross.

223
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:36,400
No, wait!

224
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,280
That's exactly what I saw!

225
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,320
So you're saying...

226
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:42,360
Yiran really got back with that rural social climber?

227
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:46,080
Yiran doesn't seem like the type to go back to an ex.

228
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:48,560
Baixi, I don't think Yiran would do that.

229
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:51,080
Oh, brother!

230
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,560
Why are you still standing there?

231
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,720
If it's broken, it needs fixing!

232
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,760
A lost cause.

233
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,760
All my hard acting went to waste.

234
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,200
Why are you here?

235
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,360
I was afraid you'd get lost.

236
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,080
I came to take you home.

237
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,960
What's wrong with you?

238
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:47,040
I'm not a kid. Why would I get lost?

239
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:49,760
Even if you're not a kid,

240
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:51,520
you can still take the wrong path sometimes.

241
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:59,800
But I don't like turning back.

242
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,120
I'll take you back, then.

243
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:13,840
Let's go.

244
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,360
Yiran

245
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,840
You... you...

246
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:05,920
I... I...

247
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,400
I just wanted to say...

248
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,360
the bankbook Granny Xiufang gave me,

249
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:10,600
I've donated to the nursing home through the community.

250
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,920
I hope lonely seniors like her...

251
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,920
can get some help.

252
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:18,000
That's... that's great.

253
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,400
I mean, if Granny Xiufang is watching from above,

254
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,920
she'd definitely be very pleased.

255
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:22,560
Yeah.

256
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,520
She definitely would.

257
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,640
I'll head up then.

258
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,920
Mister, miss.

259
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:49,120
Are you two dating?

260
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:49,920
Come here.

261
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,800
We didn't see anything.

262
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,040
Yangyang, you're not asleep yet?

263
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:55,640
We didn't see anything.

264
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:56,600
Go back, go back.

265
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:58,520
Go back, go back, go back.

266
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:00,040
Seriously.

267
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:01,560
You...

268
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:02,400
Go for it.

269
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,360
We were...

270
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:03,840
You were...

271
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,560
So frustrating.

272
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,440
My dad called me home for a midnight snack.

273
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,560
Mr. Chen, you're going the wrong way.

274
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:11,560
This way, this way.

275
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:15,160
Come again! Visit often!

276
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:16,640
Wu Huilian!

277
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:21,600
Your mouth is like a leaky teapot.

278
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:23,760
I didn't even get to see the good part.

279
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:24,760
What's there to watch?

280
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,400
You little brat.

281
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:27,720
What did you say, you brat?

282
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,000
How are things going between you two?

283
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,520
Come on, tell Mom.

284
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:32,760
What business is it of yours?

285
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,960
Just tell Mom.

286
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:37,880
Yiran, Yiran!

287
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,600
How far have you two progressed?

288
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,120
Stop asking, stop asking!

289
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:42,280
You're 26 years old.

290
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,840
It's normal to go out, right?

291
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,600
What is there to be shy about?

292
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,560
If you don't know how...

293
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:48,800
If you don't know how to kiss, Mom can teach you!

294
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,040
Yiran Star

295
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,000
So romantic!

296
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,720
A vantage point brings advantage.

297
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,920
Mr. Chen's got game.

298
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,200
What are you talking about?

299
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:18,080
If you

300
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:22,240
could end up with Mr. Chen,

301
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,640
I'll be relieved.

302
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:25,000
I'll have no regrets.

303
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,440
Worry about yourself first.

304
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:27,800
Stay out of my business.

305
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:30,160
You and Xiaofang are still young.

306
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,320
You're setting your sights

307
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:35,080
way too high.

308
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:36,320
What do you mean?

309
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:39,000
When it comes to dating and finding a partner,

310
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,600
you need to look with your heart.

311
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,800
Use your heart

312
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:47,760
to feel the people around you who bring you warmth.

313
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,160
I bought this for you online.

314
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:53,200
It's the naming rights to a star.

315
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,120
Here's the certificate.

316
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:58,480
From now on, there's a star in the sky just for you.

317
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:01,200
Even though you can't see or touch it,

318
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:04,200
it's right there.

319
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,360
Always there.

320
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,080
Look at that smile. See?

321
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:27,280
Director Liu.

322
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:29,760
Here's Granny Zhang Xiufang's anti-human trafficking feature.

323
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,400
I've finished editing it.

324
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,280
Please see if anything needs changing.

325
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,360
Care for some tea?

326
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:36,640
No, thank you.

327
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:38,520
Okay.

328
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:39,720
Have some water then.

329
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:54,160
Just leave the stuff here for now.

330
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:55,520
I'll take a look when I have time.

331
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,480
Director Liu, you know

332
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:04,000
we've poured a lot of heart into this documentary.

333
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,720
We hope to finalize it as soon as possible.

334
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,200
Plus, anti-human trafficking is a hot topic right now.

335
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,320
It's not too sensitive,

336
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:11,920
so airing it soon will draw more attention.

337
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,520
It might even save more families.

338
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:14,520
Xiao Fan,

339
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:17,080
when this documentary airs

340
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,880
is up to the station.

341
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:19,680
Besides,

342
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:22,920
it's not even certain if it will pass the review.

343
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:26,040
But you approved this project!

344
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,080
And all the procedures I followed

345
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,800
were strictly by the station's standards.

346
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:30,560
All right, all right.

347
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,480
Let's put the documentary aside for now.

348
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,640
Let me ask you, Xiao Fan.

349
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:40,520
How are the ad negotiations with your father going?

350
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:44,400
My dad hasn't decided yet.

351
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,120
Hasn't decided yet?

352
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,200
Or does he not want to decide?

353
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,040
Your work efficiency is too low.

354
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:53,400
I'm talking to you about the documentary.

355
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,600
What does my dad's ad investment

356
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:56,880
have to do with this?

357
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:59,080
Are you too naive?

358
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,600
Without ad revenue,

359
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,160
how is the station supposed to operate?

360
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,600
Does the value and result of everyone's hard work

361
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:08,520
mean less than a single ad placement?

362
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:11,960
Don't talk to me about value right now.

363
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,120
In this world,

364
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,880
revenue is value.

365
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,160
Without it, your documentary is just trash.

366
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:18,920
What do you mean?

367
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,000
Fine.

368
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:27,600
I'll make myself even clearer.

369
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:30,600
Do you think I'm doing this for you?

370
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:33,000
I'm doing this as a favor to your father.

371
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,840
The Ugly Duckling becoming a swan...

372
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:38,200
Is it because the duckling worked hard?

373
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,320
No.

374
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:43,000
It's because its parents were swans.

375
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:44,880
Hurry up and sort things out with your dad.

376
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,280
Director Liu,

377
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,040
I work for social value,

378
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,000
not to pull in ads for you.

379
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:58,400
What kind of attitude is that?

380
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:00,560
If you don't want to work, then quit!

381
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:04,640
I quit!

382
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,920
You don't deserve to watch this.

383
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:13,360
Xiao Fan!

384
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:17,240
What kind of temper tantrum is this?

385
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,880
Where can you even go if you leave the station?

386
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,000
Even if I sweep the streets,

387
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,400
I don't want to see your ugly face anymore.

388
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:35,080
You brat!

389
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,320
You're going too far!

390
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:37,200
Do you know

391
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:39,600
how much effort it took to get you into the station?

392
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,680
That was your idea.

393
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:42,680
Did you ever ask if I actually wanted it?

394
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:44,400
So many people want this job,

395
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,640
yet you couldn't care less!

396
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:47,080
Right, you've done so much for me.

397
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:48,160
Thank you.

398
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,640
You are so spoiled.

399
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:50,720
You don't know the ways of the world.

400
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:52,560
I'm going to see the world for myself.

401
00:21:52,560 --> 00:21:53,240
From now on,

402
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:55,040
I'll only do what I want to do.

403
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:57,000
You have no idea how cruel reality is.

404
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:57,680
Without connections,

405
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,400
you won't be able to achieve a single thing!

406
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:01,480
Yeah, in your eyes,

407
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,640
no matter how excellent I am,

408
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,360
I'm still just a piece of trash.

409
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,160
You've learned to talk back now!

410
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:17,840
Ever since I was little,

411
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,040
you only cared about yourself!

412
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:22,160
And your own face!

413
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:26,080
You never asked what I wanted!

414
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,920
You never cared!

415
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,600
I've endured it for over twenty years.

416
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,000
I've had enough!

417
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:39,880
You!

418
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:42,720
Fine! If you're so tough, get out of this house!

419
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:43,360
Get lost!

420
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:44,880
Get lost!

421
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,560
Baixi

422
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:15,560
Why are you here?

423
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:20,360
Last time, I told you I liked you.

424
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,320
I just wanted to ask you again...

425
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:27,440
Is there any chance for us?

426
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,280
Shiqi, I actually...

427
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,600
Let me just ask you one thing.

428
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:33,120
We've known each other for so many years.

429
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:38,440
Have you ever had feelings for me, even once?

430
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,440
Shiqi.

431
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:43,320
You're a great girl,

432
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:46,160
but I already like someone else.

433
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,000
How exactly is she better than me?

434
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:51,880
You can't compare feelings.

435
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,600
When you like someone,

436
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:56,120
you can't measure it with conditions or standards.

437
00:23:56,880 --> 00:24:00,440
Yiran can be fierce sometimes, and stubborn,

438
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,640
even a little silly.

439
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:03,520
But she...

440
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:04,520
is great just the way she is.

441
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,360
I understand.

442
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:13,000
Thanks for telling me the truth.

443
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:21,200
Ginger tea. Drink it while it's hot.

444
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,080
Don't catch a cold.

445
00:25:28,760 --> 00:25:29,560
Thank you.

446
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:32,160
I never thought there'd be a day

447
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:34,800
I'd hear you, Miss Fan,

448
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,400
say thank you to me.

449
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:38,960
I'm not Miss Fan anymore.

450
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:41,560
I've lost my home and my job.

451
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:47,520
Then you're a glutton for punishment.

452
00:25:48,200 --> 00:25:49,200
Refusing to enjoy a good life.

453
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:56,560
How could someone like you understand my situation?

454
00:25:57,560 --> 00:25:58,920
Someone like what?

455
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:04,800
I know you don't like me.

456
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:06,120
That's okay.

457
00:26:06,120 --> 00:26:07,120
I don't like you either.

458
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,080
But

459
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:13,840
I actually admire your attitude.

460
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:21,240
Li Yiran.

461
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:23,200
You know what?

462
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:25,640
Actually,

463
00:26:27,240 --> 00:26:28,480
I really envy you.

464
00:26:30,760 --> 00:26:32,320
You have the freedom

465
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:34,400
to do whatever you want.

466
00:26:37,040 --> 00:26:38,200
But I...

467
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:43,560
Actually, you're much luckier than me.

468
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,440
And you're so pretty.

469
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:46,880
Unlike me.

470
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:50,680
I have to rely on myself for everything.

471
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:55,200
Everyone has their own hidden struggles.

472
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,800
Everyone has their hardships.

473
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:57,960
It's not easy for anyone.

474
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:00,240
All we can do

475
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:04,360
is play the hand we're dealt.

476
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:10,840
But right now,

477
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:14,640
I have absolutely nothing.

478
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:16,280
You haven't lost everything.

479
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:20,760
The only thing a person truly owns is themselves.

480
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:24,400
Life is all about leveling up.

481
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:27,000
We overcome obstacles one by one.

482
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:31,120
Eventually, we'll all get to where we want to be,

483
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:34,600
and become who we want to be.

484
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:42,680
Li Yiran.

485
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:45,120
I still don't like you.

486
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:47,400
But,

487
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:50,800
I respect you.

488
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:54,680
Tomorrow is a new day.

489
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:58,960
Cheers to the youngest day of the rest of our lives.

490
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:27,520
Are you busy?

491
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:36,560
Yiran, I need to talk to you.

492
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:43,080
I found a guy.

493
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:45,640
You two are an unbelievable match.

494
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:48,080
Saturday at 5:00 PM.

495
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:49,880
At the Magpie Bridge Tea Restaurant.

496
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:51,160
You definitely won't regret it.

497
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:03,880
Dad, Brother-in-law!

498
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:05,120
I'm back!

499
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:06,880
Zhou Fang?

500
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,400
Bro Amin!

501
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:10,800
Bro Amin, come here!

502
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:11,720
Help me with this.

503
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:13,680
Here, hold this.

504
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:18,320
Zhou Fang, why did you bring so much stuff?

505
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:19,160
Are you running away from home?

506
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:19,960
Catch.

507
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:21,720
Here, Brother-in-law.

508
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,520
When I was packing up at home,

509
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:25,720
I found some items that really suit you guys.

510
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:26,960
I brought them all over.

511
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:30,640
Bro Amin.

512
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:31,560
No rush.

513
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:33,000
This is from my bookcase,

514
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,320
the set of books you had your eye on last time.

515
00:29:34,320 --> 00:29:35,400
This is for you.

516
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:36,400
Thanks.

517
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:40,560
Here, Brother-in-law.

518
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:41,760
This is...

519
00:29:42,560 --> 00:29:43,400
A phone?

520
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:46,040
Since your business is so busy now,

521
00:29:46,040 --> 00:29:47,920
you definitely need a new one.

522
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:49,120
You're really something.

523
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:51,040
Chen Baixi.

524
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:54,920
Dad, there's something for you too.

525
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:55,960
Here.

526
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:57,400
These things,

527
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:58,800
they must be kept with you

528
00:29:58,800 --> 00:29:59,960
to realize their true value.

529
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:08,800
This is a vintage sprinkled blue glaze porcelain.

530
00:30:09,280 --> 00:30:10,840
You really have an eye for this, Dad!

531
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:12,160
If these things

532
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:14,720
were kept at my place, they'd just gather dust.

533
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:17,200
Only you can recognize their true worth.

534
00:30:18,080 --> 00:30:19,120
My dad will definitely love it.

535
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:20,000
It's quite nice.

536
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:22,400
Zhou Fang, what are you up to?

537
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:23,560
Trying to win people's hearts?

538
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,080
Xiaofang.

539
00:30:29,080 --> 00:30:31,240
I'm not trying to win people's hearts.

540
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:33,560
I'm being completely sincere.

541
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:41,720
Xiaofang, you left this at my place too.

542
00:30:45,040 --> 00:30:46,360
Are you crazy?

543
00:30:46,360 --> 00:30:48,160
What are you really here for?

544
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,280
Aunt Huilan said

545
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:51,880
I need to stay close to you to have a chance.

546
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:53,840
In case someone like

547
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:56,040
Zhuang Qiang or whoever shows up around you.

548
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:57,960
What if you lose control?

549
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:59,240
I can definitely control myself.

550
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:00,440
But as for you,

551
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:02,120
I don't know if you can control yourself.

552
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:03,800
I can definitely control myself!

553
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:05,440
During our three years in college,

554
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,040
you were the only girl I ever liked.

555
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:09,360
That's because I was the only girl in our class!

556
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:11,800
But as for me,

557
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:13,080
with so many guys in the class,

558
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:14,760
I chose only you!

559
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:16,640
Enough!

560
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:18,880
Right now, this very instant...

561
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:19,800
Get lost!

562
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:21,520
Xiaofang, I...

563
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:26,880
Dad, Brother-in-law.

564
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:28,960
I'm homeless now.

565
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,520
What should I do?

566
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:31,920
I'm begging you.

567
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:32,560
Zhou Fang...

568
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:33,400
Hold on a second.

569
00:31:34,880 --> 00:31:36,960
Bro Jianguo, I need to take some time off.

570
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,000
Okay, okay.

571
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:47,280
Dad,

572
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:50,920
have you ever seen Bro Amin run like that?

573
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:53,080
I've never even seen him

574
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:54,280
this anxious before.

575
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:56,080
Nope.

576
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:59,720
At Amin's age,

577
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:02,920
it's not easy for him to be impulsive for love.

578
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:04,880
What?

579
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:06,600
Impulsive for love?

580
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:18,680
Zhang Lijuan, hardworking and virtuous!

581
00:32:18,680 --> 00:32:20,480
She has a great mindset!

582
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,240
Mindset of an 18-year-old, forever 18!

583
00:32:22,240 --> 00:32:24,640
Step right up, don't miss out on her!

584
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,560
Zhang Lijuan! Zhang Lijuan!

585
00:32:34,560 --> 00:32:35,280
Seize the opportunity!

586
00:32:35,280 --> 00:32:37,360
This is the most stylish man for miles around!

587
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:37,960
Seize the opportunity!

588
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:39,400
Whatever you do, don't miss out!

589
00:33:00,840 --> 00:33:04,040
You must be Mr. Bailong.

590
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:05,600
You must be Lijuan.

591
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:09,080
Eastern charm.

592
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:10,840
A delicate queen vibe.

593
00:33:16,400 --> 00:33:17,120
Please.

594
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:19,520
Thank you.

595
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:27,840
Ms. Lijuan,

596
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:30,680
do you like Jorge Luis Borges?

597
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:34,360
I...

598
00:33:34,360 --> 00:33:36,080
Of course I do.

599
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:39,560
Which of his poems do you like?

600
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:47,680
Mr. Bai, I can tell you're a man of culture.

601
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:53,440
Which of his poems do you like?

602
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,640
Of course, it's his...

603
00:33:57,920 --> 00:34:02,800
"What can I hold you with?"

604
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:13,360
What can I hold you with?

605
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:17,520
I offer you lean streets,

606
00:34:17,640 --> 00:34:19,360
desperate sunsets,

607
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:23,840
the moon of the jagged suburbs.

608
00:34:25,640 --> 00:34:29,920
I offer you the bitterness of a man

609
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:36,000
who has looked long and long at the lonely moon.

610
00:34:41,640 --> 00:34:43,760
What do you think?

611
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:48,960
Very classy.

612
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:54,080
My Yangyang will definitely love it.

613
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:58,280
Wait, Yangyang is...

614
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:00,320
Yangyang is my son.

615
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:05,480
He's a very kind kid.

616
00:35:06,080 --> 00:35:07,600
He just loves poetry.

617
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:09,040
You mean your...

618
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:11,080
somewhat slow son?

619
00:35:12,640 --> 00:35:13,640
What did you say?

620
00:35:13,640 --> 00:35:16,200
Yangyang, your somewhat slow son.

621
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:17,480
It's no big deal.

622
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:18,880
Everyone knows.

623
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:20,240
Say that again!

624
00:35:22,520 --> 00:35:24,520
Your slow son, right?

625
00:35:24,520 --> 00:35:25,360
Everyone knows it.

626
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:26,560
You're the slow son!

627
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:27,920
Your whole family is slow!

628
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:30,840
What's with your attitude?

629
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:31,720
Look at yourself.

630
00:35:31,720 --> 00:35:33,160
You're a forty-year-old woman.

631
00:35:33,720 --> 00:35:34,680
With a slow...

632
00:35:34,680 --> 00:35:36,240
To put it nicely, slow.

633
00:35:36,240 --> 00:35:38,280
To put it bluntly, a retarded son.

634
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:40,040
You're lucky I even looked at you!

635
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,440
Who are you calling retarded?

636
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:46,800
Apologize!

637
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:48,080
Why should I apologize to her?

638
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:49,440
Wait, who are you?

639
00:35:49,440 --> 00:35:50,320
None of your business who I am!

640
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:51,080
Apologize!

641
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:52,000
I won't!

642
00:35:54,600 --> 00:35:55,440
You...

643
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,160
You're hitting me?

644
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:58,400
I'm no delicate queen.

645
00:35:58,400 --> 00:35:59,760
I have plenty of strength!

646
00:35:59,760 --> 00:36:00,680
Hey, go easy!

647
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:02,280
Do you know this is an Armani tie?

648
00:36:02,480 --> 00:36:03,200
Armani!

649
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:04,840
Think I've never seen foreign brands?

650
00:36:07,080 --> 00:36:08,080
Armani?

651
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:10,760
It clearly says "Anima."

652
00:36:11,240 --> 00:36:12,000
Thirty-seven.

653
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,520
You didn't even take the tag off!

654
00:36:13,720 --> 00:36:15,440
What do you know, country bumpkin?

655
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:19,040
Get lost!

656
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:21,280
You're a country bumpkin too!

657
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:24,000
The two of you...

658
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,120
So uncultured.

659
00:36:25,120 --> 00:36:26,440
I won't lower myself to your level.

660
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:27,880
I won't stoop to your level!

661
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,720
I haven't even seen you smile yet.

662
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:50,400
What are you doing here?

663
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:52,080
I... I was passing by.

664
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:56,320
You don't buy that, do you?

665
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:57,680
I...

666
00:36:57,680 --> 00:36:59,600
I was worried about you.

667
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:02,640
Um, just now...

668
00:37:02,640 --> 00:37:04,360
He... he recited that poem wrong.

669
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:06,040
It should be "lean streets,"

670
00:37:06,040 --> 00:37:08,160
and... and "desperate sunsets,"

671
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:11,680
and... and the...

672
00:37:12,400 --> 00:37:13,520
I forgot too.

673
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:19,640
Forget about the sunsets

674
00:37:20,080 --> 00:37:21,400
or the moon.

675
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:23,320
Look,

676
00:37:24,760 --> 00:37:25,960
the bill's already paid.

677
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:26,800
Why don't

678
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:28,640
you sit down

679
00:37:28,960 --> 00:37:29,800
and we eat?

680
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:30,960
Okay.

681
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:41,320
Don't want it?

682
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:43,760
Give it to me.

683
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:55,800
I forgot.

684
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:57,240
You... you're vegetarian.

685
00:37:58,240 --> 00:37:59,880
Then there's nothing for you to eat here.

686
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:01,040
No, it's fine, Lijuan.

687
00:38:02,040 --> 00:38:02,880
I can eat it.

688
00:38:03,600 --> 00:38:04,640
I can eat all of this.

689
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:06,640
It's perfectly fine.

690
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:07,760
Are you sure?

691
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:09,400
Here.

692
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:13,800
Thank you.

693
00:38:22,200 --> 00:38:22,720
Eat up.

694
00:38:22,720 --> 00:38:23,680
I... Let me peel a shrimp for you.

695
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:48,760
Ranran

696
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:55,200
Ranran

697
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:59,240
I know it might not be appropriate to say this now,

698
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:02,520
but my mom really wants to see you again.

699
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:03,920
Just to have a meal together.

700
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:05,560
Zhuang Qiang,

701
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:08,080
did you treat what I told you a few days ago

702
00:39:08,080 --> 00:39:09,440
like it was complete bullshit?

703
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:11,400
I'm here for work,

704
00:39:11,480 --> 00:39:13,040
not because I want to see you.

705
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:14,520
I'm really hurting right now.

706
00:39:14,880 --> 00:39:16,000
Can't you just...

707
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:17,080
No.

708
00:39:17,440 --> 00:39:18,400
Ranran, listen to me.

709
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:18,840
Please give me one more chance, okay?

710
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:19,640
Let go!

711
00:39:19,640 --> 00:39:20,200
Ranran!

712
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,280
Ranran, listen to me!

713
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:22,640
Let go of her.

714
00:39:23,280 --> 00:39:24,240
Who are you?

715
00:39:24,880 --> 00:39:26,080
Our relationship

716
00:39:26,120 --> 00:39:27,080
is none of your business!

717
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:29,640
Of course it's my business.

718
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:38,320
Ranran.

719
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:40,920
I'll be staying here for a while.

720
00:39:41,440 --> 00:39:42,640
We'll see each other again.

721
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,120
So what if you're tall?

722
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:52,400
Country bumpkin.

723
00:39:54,520 --> 00:39:55,480
Let's get out of here.

724
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:07,000
Are you okay?

725
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:09,320
I'm just disgusted with my past self.

726
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:11,360
How did I ever fall for him?

727
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:14,400
Don't be so hard on your past self.

728
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:16,240
You need to look ahead.

729
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:21,840
Look ahead.

730
00:40:27,960 --> 00:40:30,000
Right, this is for you.

731
00:40:33,120 --> 00:40:36,240
Our work involves dealing with bodies a lot, right?

732
00:40:36,240 --> 00:40:38,880
It has mugwort and cloves in it.

733
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:41,680
If you ever smell something unpleasant,

734
00:40:41,680 --> 00:40:42,600
you can just take a sniff of this.

735
00:40:43,720 --> 00:40:44,680
Don't mind if I do.

736
00:40:48,120 --> 00:40:50,320
You can also get free refills from me.

737
00:40:58,080 --> 00:40:58,720
Let's go.

738
00:41:00,800 --> 00:41:02,040
It just looks very round.

739
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,360
Right, and red.

740
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:10,360
What brings you here?

741
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:15,760
I came to say goodbye.

742
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:18,960
Are you going somewhere?

743
00:41:19,800 --> 00:41:21,800
I plan to go teach in the northwest.

744
00:41:22,240 --> 00:41:24,480
Volunteer teaching? That's sudden.

745
00:41:26,640 --> 00:41:28,040
I just suddenly figured it out.

746
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:29,880
In this life,

747
00:41:29,880 --> 00:41:31,960
you have to figure out what you want to do, right?

748
00:41:33,120 --> 00:41:34,640
I was too naive before.

749
00:41:34,640 --> 00:41:37,320
I didn't know the gifts bestowed by fate

750
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:39,880
had their prices secretly marked from the start.

751
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:43,120
As for me, I've always been a spectator in other people's plays,

752
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:45,240
and lived according to other people's plans.

753
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:49,320
But I've figured it out now.

754
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:51,080
Life isn't meant to be lived for others,

755
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:52,400
it belongs to you.

756
00:41:53,320 --> 00:41:55,600
I'm ready to walk my own path.

757
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:56,880
To teach in the northwest.

758
00:41:57,760 --> 00:42:00,440
To take the world I've seen and known,

759
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:02,520
and tell the children there about it.

760
00:42:03,080 --> 00:42:05,640
Tell them what the world outside the mountains is like.

761
00:42:05,640 --> 00:42:08,360
And tell them that even if they are in the gutter,

762
00:42:08,640 --> 00:42:09,880
they should still look up at the stars.

763
00:42:11,920 --> 00:42:13,240
Even if...

764
00:42:14,560 --> 00:42:16,080
even if there's only one child

765
00:42:16,080 --> 00:42:17,360
who, because of what I say,

766
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:19,040
gets a little more light in their eyes,

767
00:42:20,520 --> 00:42:21,880
then it'll be worth it.

768
00:42:26,040 --> 00:42:27,800
Being able to do what you want to do...

769
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:28,560
I'm happy for you.

770
00:42:37,600 --> 00:42:38,040
I never expected

771
00:42:38,040 --> 00:42:40,480
to finally hold your hand this way.

772
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:50,200
I'll definitely make a difference teaching this time.

773
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:51,800
You guys keep up the good work, too.

774
00:42:51,800 --> 00:42:54,040
Don't let it be that when I return,

775
00:42:54,040 --> 00:42:55,160
you're still stuck in the same place.

776
00:42:58,840 --> 00:43:00,440
We'll do our best.

777
00:43:00,840 --> 00:43:02,080
Take good care of yourself.

778
00:43:10,480 --> 00:43:11,600
Let's both work hard.

779
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:12,560
Until we meet again.

780
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:41,120
Sweet as Honey

781
00:43:41,120 --> 00:43:44,680
I smile as sweet as honey

782
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:49,320
I just thought you were feeling a bit empty.

783
00:43:49,320 --> 00:43:49,960
Here.

784
00:43:51,040 --> 00:43:53,280
A perfect match, all set up.

785
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:55,640
Aunt Huilan,

786
00:43:55,640 --> 00:43:56,640
Mr. Zhou.

787
00:43:56,640 --> 00:43:58,520
Well, I listened to your advice.

788
00:43:58,520 --> 00:44:01,040
I've now infiltrated enemy lines.

789
00:44:01,040 --> 00:44:03,840
You can't win the tigress without entering her lair.

790
00:44:03,840 --> 00:44:06,200
That move of yours was really brilliant.

791
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:10,840
Soon, I'll be able to fully infiltrate Xiaofang's life.

792
00:44:12,200 --> 00:44:13,440
Mr. Zhou,

793
00:44:13,920 --> 00:44:16,560
It's obvious you're a smart guy.

794
00:44:16,560 --> 00:44:19,360
You learn fast and catch on quick.

795
00:44:21,280 --> 00:44:22,200
But Old Wu,

796
00:44:23,160 --> 00:44:27,000
you should also care about Yiran's situation outside of work.

797
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:29,720
What's wrong with Yiran?

798
00:44:30,400 --> 00:44:32,680
Her scumbag ex-boyfriend,

799
00:44:32,680 --> 00:44:33,360
you know him, right?

800
00:44:33,360 --> 00:44:33,920
The gold digger.

801
00:44:33,920 --> 00:44:35,000
That shameless guy.

802
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:35,760
Damn.

803
00:44:36,640 --> 00:44:37,480
Country bumpkin!

804
00:44:38,080 --> 00:44:39,440
You think being tall makes you special?

805
00:44:50,400 --> 00:44:52,480
Did you know he's back from Shanghai?

806
00:44:52,480 --> 00:44:54,040
He came back to get back together with Yiran.

807
00:44:54,040 --> 00:44:55,360
I ran into him a couple of days ago.

808
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:56,680
He held onto Yiran and wouldn't let go.

809
00:44:56,680 --> 00:44:58,480
There was nothing Yiran could do.

810
00:44:58,960 --> 00:45:00,280
She was scared to tears.

811
00:45:10,720 --> 00:45:11,800
Th- That...

812
00:45:12,320 --> 00:45:13,440
Son of a bitch!

813
00:45:13,440 --> 00:45:15,600
I'm gonna go beat up that son of a bitch!

814
00:45:15,800 --> 00:45:16,520
Calm down!

815
00:45:16,520 --> 00:45:17,400
Don't stop me!

816
00:45:18,560 --> 00:45:19,240
You can't! You can't!

817
00:45:19,640 --> 00:45:20,480
Don't hold me back!

818
00:45:20,480 --> 00:45:21,440
Don't hold me back!

819
00:45:22,440 --> 00:45:23,560
Calm down!
